WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.480
Follow the energy path into the rack, then follow the heat out.

2
00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:07.800
Power passes through conversion and distribution stages before reaching the workload.

3
00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:12.680
Each stage has limits, losses, protection behavior and an operating envelope.

4
00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:16.520
A rating at one stage doesn't establish what reaches the equipment after

5
00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:18.020
every other constraint is applied.

6
00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:22.500
For cooling, identify both the liquid path and the residual air path.

7
00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:25.980
The rack may connect to a coolant distribution unit, or C D

8
00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:28.000
U, with a separate facility-side loop.

9
00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:32.040
Don't assume those fluids, pressures or temperatures are interchangeable.

10
00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:35.980
A thermal boundary needs a defined condition and a responsible party on

11
00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:36.540
each side.

12
00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:41.080
This first map doesn't require detailed electrical or hydraulic calculations.

13
00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:43.260
It requires the boundaries to be visible.

14
00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:48.000
Mark where the facility commitment ends, where the rack integrator's responsibility begins,

15
00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:50.100
and what the equipment supplier assumes.

16
00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:53.920
If two parties each assume the other provides the same function, the

17
00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:56.340
diagram has exposed a real integration risk.

18
00:00:56.760 --> 00:01:00.820
Resolve that gap before turning individual component ratings into a system claim.

